  "body": "Closes #3286\n\n### Problem\nWhen composing text with an IME in `InputBaseState` (e.g., `Textarea` or `Input`), newly inserted or marked text offsets may not yet be shaped in `last_layout` prior to the subsequent repaint. In `bounds_for_range`, querying `line.position_for_index` for offsets outside `last_layout` returns `None`.\n\nPreviously, `start_origin` and `end_origin` both fell back via `unwrap_or_default()`, resetting their origins to `(0, 0)`. This caused:\n1. Candidate windows to jump horizontally back to the input origin before repainting.\n2. If `start_origin` was resolved within `last_layout` but `end_origin` fell past the layout, `end_origin` defaulted to `(0, 0)`, producing inverted or full-width bounds.\n\n### Solution\n1. In `bounds_for_range`, when `start_origin` cannot be resolved within `last_layout`, fall back to the position of `self.last_cursor` (or `self.cursor()`) from the previous layout.\n2. Default `end_origin` to `start_origin` rather than `(0, 0)` so that unresolved end offsets remain anchored at the caret rather than jumping to the left margin.\n3. Added a regression unit test `test_ime_candidate_bounds_fallback_before_repaint` validating that candidate bounds stay within proximity of the caret before repaint.\n",
